  "_comment": "QueryPerformanceCounter: the IAT slot 0x100400dc points at a 33-byte stdcall stub at 0x100276ad, in the padding between MeasureCpuClock (ends 0x100276ac) and ReadTimestampCounter (0x100276d0). It is a passthrough callee, so it runs for real. The stub stores the next u32 of the counter table to the low dword of *arg, zeroes the high dword, and advances the index cell. Its two absolute addresses (0x100276b3, 0x100276c7) are patched with the address of the 'qpc' object: index cell at +0x40 (starts at +0x80), counter table at +0x80 (u32 each, 4 bytes apart). The return value is not set: neither side reads EAX after the call. writes hex takes one value per callee, not a per-call list, so each case's counter timeline is a memory table; the top-level table is the default, and a case's table overwrites its first entries (top-level memory is written before case memory). Per sample: base, base+50 (first wait exits), base+50+window (second wait exits). RDTSC cycles per sample = rdtsc_step x that sample's do-while iterations; at 1 MHz a window of W ticks is W microseconds.",
